cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its archived data, please cite the versioned Zenodo release."
title: "HAXS: stochastic moving-occupancy XXZ screening and reproducibility package"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-12
repository-code: "https://github.com/Subhojith90/HAXS"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  HAXS is the code-and-data reproducibility release for a predeclared
  fixed-time spin-squeezing-parameter contrast in a 3x3x3 stochastic
  moving-occupancy XXZ surrogate. It includes simulation and analysis code,
  configurations, tests, dependency locks, deterministic figure generation,
  complete source tables, and publication-closure evidence. The unpublished
  manuscript is not included in this software release.
keywords:
  - spin squeezing
  - XXZ magnet
  - discrete truncated Wigner approximation
  - stochastic occupancy
  - hierarchical bootstrap
  - reproducible simulation
